  "extreme_width_difference_note": "15 of 412 patients with estimable width differ by more than 0.05 in percentile-interval width, the largest by 0.6816. Every one of them already had a receipt width of at least 0.2738, i.e. above the 0.2 released bound, so none of them was classified RELIABLE by either stream. Their released status is NOT always identical, however: 2 of the 15 flipped, including the worst case (IMPRECISE -> SIGN_UNSTABLE). The wide-interval tail is therefore where the two streams agree least, which is also where the index is least informative under either stream.",
